  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>invoices_base64 - the same invoice reader, with the images encoded as Base64 in the stream first, as
images from a database or an API arrive.
Needs Ollama with ${VISION_MODEL} (gemma3:12b) and the GenAI plugins with a GENAI-EE license.

1. gfn-invoices: Get File Names, ../invoices, wildcard .*\.(png|jpg), one row per image (filename,
   short_filename).
2. b64-image: Base64 Encoder, Source - Stream, Format File, field filename; result image_b64.
3. const-instruction: Add constants, run_instruction (the same JSON instruction as invoices_vision) and
   message.
4. ai-invoice: AI Chat; Stream message message, run instruction run_instruction; Attach Document(s),
   Stream, Field Format Image (Base64 Encoded), field image_b64; Ollama ${VISION_MODEL} at
   ${OLLAMA_URL}, temperature 0, numCtx 4096, timeout 300; result llm_json.
5. json-invoice: JSON input from llm_json: the nine fields.
6. js-validate: Modified JavaScript value, difference = subtotal + tax - total; needs_review when it is over
   0.01, an amount is missing, or is_invoice is false.
7. sv-results: Select values, the file name, the nine fields and the three check fields (image_b64 is left out).
8. txt-results: Text file output, invoice_results_base64.csv beside this file.

Parameters: VISION_MODEL gemma3:12b, OLLAMA_URL http://localhost:11434.
Shipped data: 7 images (6 invoices and receipts, 1 meeting agenda); invoice_truth.csv holds the printed
figures.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>619</width>
      <heigth>386</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
